of children to environmental tobacco smoke (ETS) by different methods</article-title><source>Human experimental toxicology</source><year>1999</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>297</fpage><lpage>301</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10333318</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1191/096032799678840075</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Borland</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Mullins</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Trotter</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trends in environmental tobacco smoke restrictions in the home in Victoria, Australia</article-title><source>Tobacco Control</source><year>1999</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>266</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10599570</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/tc.8.3.266</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>